        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='width:100%;height:100%;overflow:auto;box-sizing:border-box;container-type:inline-size;background:#eef4fb;font-family:system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#182d4c'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5cqw,40px) 64px'><div style='padding-top:32px'><header data-role='masthead'><div style='padding:10px 0;border-top:6px solid #294b83;border-bottom:1px solid #182d4c;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>PRIMITIVE · glyph</div><h1 style='margin:40px 0 0;font:850 clamp(36px,9.5cqw,72px)/.98 system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.035em;text-wrap:balance;color:#182d4c'>Glyph</h1><p style='margin:18px 0 0;max-width:36ch;font:400 clamp(20px,3.6cqw,26px)/1.4 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#46617f'>The small mark that stands for a node or graph, and the last step of a Surface.</p></header></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><div style='display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-start;gap:32px 40px'><div style='flex:999 1 380px;min-width:0'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Meaning</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>A Glyph is a node’s mark: the small symbol that stands for it when it is too far away or too small to read. Every chain of faces ends in one. It is a named icon (a house, a gear, a star), a single character like § or ⚑ (drawn in a font of your choice), or an emoji. A glyph is not a face. It has no page to show, only a mark. Encoding: a <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>glyph</code> node; the root may also hold a fallback mark in <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>data.glyph</code>. It is its own primitive, with its own editor.</p></section></div><div style='flex:1 1 220px;min-width:0'><section data-role='settings' style='padding-top:10px;border-top:3px solid #182d4c'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#182d4c'>At a glance</h2><dl style='margin:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:max-content 1fr;column-gap:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #a6bed9'><dt style='padding:9px 0 9px;border-top:1px solid #a6bed9;font:400 13px/20px system-ui;color:#46617f'>Node type</dt><dd style='margin:0;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid #a6bed9;text-align:right;font:600 14px/20px system-ui;color:#182d4c;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>glyph</dd><dt style='padding:9px 0 9px;border-top:1px solid #a6bed9;font:400 13px/20px system-ui;color:#46617f'>Shown when browsing</dt><dd style='margin:0;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid #a6bed9;text-align:right;font:600 14px/20px system-ui;color:#182d4c;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>No, only when editing</dd><dt style='grid-column:1/-1;padding:9px 0 0px;border-top:1px solid #a6bed9;font:400 13px/20px system-ui;color:#46617f'>Encoded as</dt><dd style='grid-column:1/-1;margin:0;padding:2px 0 9px;font:600 14px/20px system-ui;color:#182d4c;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>a glyph node; the root may hold a fallback mark</dd></dl></section></div></div></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Invariants</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>A face may render glyph-shaped artwork without being named Icon. It is still a face. Every authored Surface starts with at least one face and ends in its ordinary Glyph; the terminal Glyph does not replace the face.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>The terminal belongs to the selected track. Never select another Surface’s glyph merely because it appears first in the file.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Contract</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>TypeGlyph reads named icon definitions <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>{kind: &quot;icon&quot;, name}</code>, text/symbol definitions with value/symbol/name, as object definitions. An older graph may contain a bare string, but TypeGlyph does not treat a bare string as an authored icon or symbol object. Text is limited to one grapheme by getSingleCharacterGlyph. Readers differ: surfaceChains extracts object glyph definitions; callers retain compatibility fallbacks. Do not assume every reader accepts every older form identically.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>A character mark is <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>{kind: &quot;symbol&quot;, value}</code>, and may add <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>font</code> (a Google Fonts family name) and <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>bold</code>. Without a font it is drawn in bold Georgia, as it always was; with one it is drawn at its regular weight unless <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>bold</code> is true, and falls back to the Georgia look when the font cannot be had. A mark may also carry its own <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>color</code>, which shows where the place drawing it has not chosen one. An emoji is a symbol whose value is the emoji; it is drawn in colour by the system and ignores <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>color</code> and <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>font</code>.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Ports and Relationships</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>A Glyph has one port, <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>root</code>, and the last <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>next-face</code> edge of a Surface chain lands on it, from the last face’s <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>sequence-out</code>. Glyph has no <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>sequence-out</code>: nothing comes after the mark.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Behavior</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>TypeGlyph resolves known icon names and symbolic characters. collectSurfaceChains stops at the first Glyph and diagnoses continuation; resolveSurfaceGlyph selects the terminal mark and declared fallback.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Known gaps</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>Bare-string compatibility belongs to the concrete reader; current object-only extraction in surfaceChains means broad claims of universal string support need a dedicated regression. The smallest workspace representation’s interaction policy remains a product question, not a reason to add a title bar to Glyph.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'><strong>Still open.</strong> The workspace interaction policy at terminal Glyph scale is still open. The accepted boundary is that a face drawing glyph-shaped artwork remains a face, and a terminal Glyph does not get a graph title bar. This spec does not decide new glyph zoom/navigation behavior.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Representations</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>A glyph is symbolic artwork. A face can render the same artwork while keeping a face’s chrome and meaning. A selected representation uses the existing workspace frame. Surface and resolution changes do not implicitly resize it, reflow neighbors or change camera zoom. Focusing a graph draws it at its own authored size, whatever size it was dragged to in the workspace while it was not focused; that workspace size is kept for when focus leaves and never changes the graph. Manual resizing is explicit: on a focused graph it sets the graph’s own window, on an unfocused one only its size in this workspace.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Explicitly Not Part of This Primitive</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>Not a face (not even one named Icon), not a replacement for a required face, and not authority to navigate or mutate.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Examples</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>Try it:</p><ol style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:26px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Switch to edit mode (the pencil).</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Press Add node and choose Glyph. A card with a small mark appears.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Select it and press Edit, or double-click it. The card turns into the editor.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Leave the kind on Material icon and type in the search box, say &quot;star&quot;. Pick one from the grid and the card changes.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Change the kind to Character and pick a symbol from the map, or type or paste one. Open the Font tab and choose a font from Google Fonts: each tile shows your character in that font.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Change the kind to Emoji and pick one. An emoji keeps its own colours.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Choose a colour, then press Done or Esc to put the card back. Clicking elsewhere does the same. The chain of the Page Template ends in a Glyph named Arrival.</li></ol></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Where this lives</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>Source (twilite repository):</p><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/components/TypeGlyph.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/utils/glyphDefinition.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/utils/surfaceChains.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/utils/portDeclarations.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/utils/glyphFonts.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/Nodes/GlyphInlineEditor.js</code></li></ul><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>Focused tests (twilite repository):</p><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/glyphDefinition.test.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/surfaceChains.test.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/hitboxGlyph.test.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/glyphInlineEditor.test.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/glyphCharacters.test.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/glyphFonts.test.js</code></li></ul><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>These pointers identify evidence to inspect. Structural validation does not prove runtime or browser behavior.</p></section></div></div></div>"
        },
