    {
      "id": "glyph-meaning",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Meaning",
      "position": {
        "x": -530,
        "y": -300
      },
      "width": 720,
      "height": 380,
      "data": {
        "title": "Meaning",
        "body": "A Glyph is a node’s mark: the small symbol that stands for it when it is too far away or too small to read. Every chain of faces ends in one. It is a named icon (a house, a gear, a star), a single character like § or ⚑ (drawn in a font of your choice), or an emoji. A glyph is not a face. It has no page to show, only a mark. Encoding: a `glyph` node; the root may also hold a fallback mark in `data.glyph`. It is its own primitive, with its own editor.",
