    {
      "id": "glyph-contract",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Contract",
      "position": {
        "x": 1150,
        "y": -300
      },
      "width": 720,
      "height": 380,
      "data": {
        "title": "Contract",
        "body": "TypeGlyph reads named icon definitions `{kind: \"icon\", name}`, text/symbol definitions with value/symbol/name, as object definitions. An older graph may contain a bare string, but TypeGlyph does not treat a bare string as an authored icon or symbol object. Text is limited to one grapheme by getSingleCharacterGlyph. Readers differ: surfaceChains extracts object glyph definitions; callers retain compatibility fallbacks. Do not assume every reader accepts every older form identically.\n\nA character mark is `{kind: \"symbol\", value}`, and may add `font` (a Google Fonts family name) and `bold`. Without a font it is drawn in bold Georgia, as it always was; with one it is drawn at its regular weight unless `bold` is true, and falls back to the Georgia look when the font cannot be had. A mark may also carry its own `color`, which shows where the place drawing it has not chosen one. An emoji is a symbol whose value is the emoji; it is drawn in colour by the system and ignores `color` and `font`.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "bridge",
          "updatedAt": 1791592063633,
          "reason": "bridge-reference"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-glyph"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
