    {
      "id": "glyph-examples",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Examples",
      "position": {
        "x": 1990,
        "y": 200
      },
      "width": 720,
      "height": 380,
      "data": {
        "title": "Examples",
        "body": "Try it:\n1. Switch to edit mode (the pencil).\n2. Press Add node and choose Glyph. A card with a small mark appears.\n3. Select it and press Edit, or double-click it. The card turns into the editor.\n4. Leave the kind on Material icon and type in the search box, say \"star\". Pick one from the grid and the card changes.\n5. Change the kind to Character and pick a symbol from the map, or type or paste one. Open the Font tab and choose a font from Google Fonts: each tile shows your character in that font.\n6. Change the kind to Emoji and pick one. An emoji keeps its own colours.\n7. Choose a colour, then press Done or Esc to put the card back. Clicking elsewhere does the same.\nThe chain of the Page Template ends in a Glyph named Arrival.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
